# Coding style

## Rules

- Smallest correct change that solves the asked problem.
- Reuse existing helpers/patterns before adding new ones.
- No speculative abstractions, “flex” layers, or unused config.
- Deletion over addition when cleaning dead code you touched.
- One concern per PR/change when practical.
- Match naming and folder conventions already in the repo.
- Leave one small test or self-check for non-trivial logic.

## DO / DON'T

```text
✅ Fix the shared function once (all callers benefit)
✅ Validate at trust boundaries; handle errors that prevent data loss
❌ Extra wrappers “for later”
❌ New dependency if stdlib or existing dep works
❌ Drive-by refactors unrelated to the task
❌ Essays in comments — only why, when non-obvious
```

Ponytail note: if you cut a corner with a known ceiling, mark `// ponytail: <ceiling>; upgrade: <path>`.
